@startuml
title Deadlock Playground - Resource Request Sequence

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #444444
  LifeLineBorderColor #777777
  ParticipantBorderColor #444444
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F7F7F7
  ActorBorderColor #444444
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #777777
  GroupBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
}

hide footbox
autonumber

actor User
participant "Browser\nAPI Client" as Client
participant "ApiServer" as API
participant "SessionStore" as Store
participant "SimulationEngine" as Engine
participant "Process" as Process
participant "Resource" as Resource
participant "SafetyChecker" as Safety
participant "History" as History

alt Manual request

  User -> Client : Select process, resource and count
  User -> Client : Click Request
  Client -> API : POST /api/request\n{process, resource, count}

else Scheduled request

  User -> Client : Click Step
  Client -> API : POST /api/step\n{}

  note over API,Engine
    This sequence follows the REQUEST
    operation selected by Step.

    Hold and Wait prevention may require
    an atomic group of scripted requests.
  end note

end

API -> Store : Resolve browser session
Store --> API : Session-specific engine

API -> Engine : Execute resource request

Engine -> Process : Inspect process state,\nholdings and pending operations
Process --> Engine : Current process information

Engine -> Resource : Inspect resource capacity\nand shareability
Resource --> Engine : Current resource information

Engine -> Engine : Validate request and active prevention rules

alt Invalid request or declared values

  Engine --> API : Validation error

  note over Engine,History
    Reject invalid input without
    changing state or history.
  end note

else Manual prevention violation

  Engine --> API : Prevention rejection

  note over Engine,History
    A rejected manual prevention
    request leaves state and
    history unchanged.
  end note

else Scripted prevention violation

  Engine -> Process : Stop invalid script
  Engine -> Process : Set state to TERMINATED
  Engine -> Resource : Return process holdings

  Engine -> History : Commit applicable state events\nand restorable snapshot

  Engine --> API : Report scripted violation\nand resulting state

else Request passes validation and prevention

  Engine -> Engine : Determine requested quantity\nor atomic request group

  Engine -> Resource : Check effective available capacity

  note over Engine,Resource
    When Mutual Exclusion prevention
    is enabled, resources configured
    as shareable do not consume
    exclusive available capacity.

    Other resources use normal
    instance accounting.
  end note

  alt Insufficient capacity

    opt Release When Blocked enabled

      Engine -> Process : Identify existing holdings
      Engine -> Resource : Return held instances
      Engine -> Process : Preserve demand for atomic reacquisition

    end

    Engine -> Process : Record pending request or group
    Engine -> Process : Set state to WAITING

    Engine -> Engine : Reconsider eligible waiters\nif holdings were returned

    Engine -> History : Commit applicable BLOCK,\nrelease and state events

    Engine --> API : BLOCKED\nUpdated simulation state

  else Capacity available or effective sharing allowed

    alt Banker's avoidance enabled

      Engine -> Engine : Validate request against\ndeclared maximum claim

      alt Request exceeds declared claim

        Engine --> API : Validation error

        note over Engine,History
          No allocation or history
          change is committed.
        end note

      else Request within declared claim

        Engine -> Safety : Evaluate tentative allocation\nand remaining resource needs

        Safety --> Engine : SafetyResult

        alt Safe state

          Engine -> Resource : Grant requested instances
          Engine -> Process : Update holdings and execution progress

          Engine -> Engine : Apply completion and\nresulting state changes

          Engine -> History : Commit AVOIDANCE_CHECK,\nGRANT and applicable state events

          Engine --> API : GRANTED\nSafe sequence and updated state

        else Unsafe state

          Engine -> Process : Record pending request
          Engine -> Process : Set state to WAITING

          note over Engine,Process
            Tentative grant is not applied.
            Existing holdings are preserved.

            The pending request can be
            reconsidered when resources
            become available.
          end note

          Engine -> History : Commit unsafe AVOIDANCE_CHECK\nand applicable waiting events

          Engine --> API : DENIED_UNSAFE\nReason and updated state

        end

      end

    else Banker's avoidance disabled

      Engine -> Resource : Grant requested instances
      Engine -> Process : Update holdings and execution progress

      Engine -> Engine : Apply completion and\nresulting state changes

      Engine -> History : Commit GRANT and\napplicable state events

      Engine --> API : GRANTED\nUpdated simulation state

      note over Engine,History
        Demo mode does not reject
        an allocation merely because
        the resulting state is unsafe.
      end note

    end

  end

end

API --> Client : JSON response and current state

Client -> Client : Synchronize graph, processes,\nresources and event history

Client --> User : Display request outcome

note over Engine,History
  Committed events reference coherent
  snapshots of the resulting state.

  A successful new command from an
  earlier historical position may
  replace the obsolete future.

  Rejected commands without committed
  effects preserve existing history.
end note

@enduml
